  "summary": "Threat actors chained CVE-2026-88771 and CVE-2026-88779 to gain root access on Citrix NetScaler appliances. The malware, dubbed SLAPSHOT, establishes persistence via cron, rc scripts, and web shells, and uses the compromised device as a pivot point for internal reconnaissance. A separate Go-based proxy named nsvmd was also deployed for C2.",
